    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319-a1">

                <pb facs="0600" n="552" xml:id="pg552"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Schuyler to Mr.
                            Maynard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1877-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 24, 1877</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my previous reports I hare the
                    honor to inclose to you the project for the administrative autonomy of Bulgaria,
                    as agreed upon in the preliminary conferences, and presented for the acceptance
                    of the Porte at the first meeting of the plenary conference. With the exception
                    of dividing Bulgaria into two districts, it is, in other language, substantially
                    the same as the project prepared by Prince Tseretelef and myself. I inclose also
                    the minimum or ultimatum which was rejected by the Porte at the final meeting of
                    the conference, which is in fact a mere <hi rendition="#italic">résumé</hi> of
                    the project without any important concession.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>EUGENE SCHUYLER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
